Campfire wasm patch 0106: export the owner key ("Show owner key").

A BEAM node started with a wallet's owner key (beam-node --owner_key=<key>
--pass=<password>) recognises every coin of that seed in the blocks it
processes, offline and max-privacy payments included. The key lets the node
see balances and history; it cannot spend. BEAM's CLI exports it with
`beam-wallet export_owner_key` and the desktop and Android wallets through
WalletClient::exportOwnerKey; the wasm client had no way to.

This adds WasmWalletClient.exportOwnerKey(pass, cb) on a running wallet. On
the wallet thread, which owns the database, it exports the owner Kdf exactly
as those do: KeyString with the password `pass`, meta "0", ExportP. The web
app opens wallet.db with a random database password, so `pass` is the
password the person typed, and the node must be started with that same
--pass. cb(key) runs on the main thread; cb(null) when the wallet is not
running or the export failed. The callback is kept on the main thread (a val
must not be released on another one), and the call is dropped if the client
object is deleted first. Neither the password nor the key is logged.

